{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
PEELING BACK THE LAYERS

26
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:38,025
[suspenseful violin music playing]

27
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:47,993
- And who might you be?
- I'm here from Horns Pharmaceuticals.

28
00:02:01,841 --> 00:02:03,509
[squeaking]

29
00:02:05,094 --> 00:02:06,220
[researcher] This way.

30
00:02:06,804 --> 00:02:08,806
[clicking]

31
00:02:14,937 --> 00:02:16,730
You must be Chief Deshico.

32
00:02:16,814 --> 00:02:19,483
My name is Garmo,
from Horns Pharmaceuticals.

33
00:02:20,359 --> 00:02:21,277
Pleasure.

34
00:02:22,111 --> 00:02:23,445
Is this urgent?

35
00:02:23,529 --> 00:02:25,614
In fact, it's a matter of life and death.

36
00:02:26,282 --> 00:02:30,369
I assume you're aware of the incidents
involving young carnivores lately.

37
00:02:30,953 --> 00:02:31,954
Yes.

38
00:02:32,037 --> 00:02:33,372
Have a look at this.

39
00:02:33,455 --> 00:02:36,208
The substances used in Kines
may be the culprit.

40
00:02:38,169 --> 00:02:39,003
Oh?

41
00:02:40,171 --> 00:02:43,424
[Louis] Myosin, actin, and myogen.
You see?

42
00:02:44,466 --> 00:02:45,885
[Deshico] Those are meat proteins.

43
00:02:45,968 --> 00:02:46,844
Indeed.

44
00:02:47,595 --> 00:02:50,973
Imagine my surprise to find them
in an energy drink of all places.

45
00:02:51,473 --> 00:02:53,392
However, there are only trace amounts,

46
00:02:53,475 --> 00:02:56,061
not enough for consumption
to trigger a reaction.

47
00:02:56,812 --> 00:03:00,858
Which suggests they may be reacting
with something carnivores naturally have,

48
00:03:00,941 --> 00:03:03,402
affecting some kind
of neural functionality.

49
00:03:03,485 --> 00:03:05,779
- I suppose you found something?
- Yes.

50
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,282
I found your research paper.

51
00:03:08,365 --> 00:03:10,993
- Ah! You read that?
- Yes.

52
00:03:11,702 --> 00:03:14,705
Though I couldn't immediately accept
your conclusions.

53
00:03:14,788 --> 00:03:16,707
Mmm. [laughs]

54
00:03:17,374 --> 00:03:18,667
Well, you don't say.

55
00:03:18,751 --> 00:03:19,585
[snarls softly]

56
00:03:20,252 --> 00:03:21,754
May I borrow that Kines?

57
00:03:22,713 --> 00:03:23,756
Take it.

58
00:03:23,839 --> 00:03:25,841
[whirring]

59
00:03:27,509 --> 00:03:29,136
All right.

60
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:32,139
Now, this sample
is from a regular carnivore.

61
00:03:32,806 --> 00:03:35,559
And you'll see, when I add in the Kines...

62
00:03:38,479 --> 00:03:41,649
Mmm, no real change, is there?

63
00:03:41,732 --> 00:03:42,650
Right.

64
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:45,069
Okay. Where is...

65
00:03:45,152 --> 00:03:46,695
Ah! Here we are.

66
00:03:46,779 --> 00:03:50,991
This next sample is from a carnivore
who routinely eats real meat.

67
00:03:51,575 --> 00:03:53,702
When I add Kines to this...

68
00:03:56,455 --> 00:03:57,289
[Louis gasps]

69
00:03:57,790 --> 00:04:01,710
[Deshico] GST isozymes remain in the body
long after meat has been consumed.

70
00:04:02,336 --> 00:04:04,004
If you have those GSTs,

71
00:04:04,088 --> 00:04:07,466
they bind to the proteins in Kines
and become a fusion protein.

72
00:04:07,549 --> 00:04:11,220
It's like eating a large amount of meat
without having to touch a spec of flesh.

73
00:04:11,303 --> 00:04:13,555
So, if we can stop it
from binding together, then--

74
00:04:13,639 --> 00:04:16,183
Mmm-mmm. No, no.
Why would we ruin a good thing?

75
00:04:16,267 --> 00:04:19,186
[splutters] Because this is dangerous.

76
00:04:19,270 --> 00:04:21,272
- We can't leave this out there.
- [grunts]

77
00:04:21,772 --> 00:04:22,815
Here's the thing.

78
00:04:23,399 --> 00:04:27,653
In our society, eating real meat
is strictly forbidden, right?

79
00:04:27,736 --> 00:04:29,488
Right.

80
00:04:29,571 --> 00:04:32,616
Okay, then. So, nobody is doing it,
are they?

81
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:37,121
Which means, it should be perfectly fine
to drink one of these.

82
00:04:37,204 --> 00:04:40,416
- Theoretically, yes, but realistically--
- Oh, dear!

83
00:04:40,499 --> 00:04:42,584
So you can't approve of Kines,

84
00:04:42,668 --> 00:04:45,170
but you can ignore
illegal meat consumption?

85
00:04:45,254 --> 00:04:46,547
Uh, no, that's--

86
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:49,717
Carnivores and herbivores coexisting
is simply twisted,

87
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:53,262
and Kines is an experimental drug
that'll bring this to light.

88
00:04:53,345 --> 00:04:54,972
Doesn't that intrigue you?

89
00:04:55,055 --> 00:04:57,433
No! Are you insane? This is wrong!

90
00:04:57,516 --> 00:05:00,185
Yes. Very wrong, indeed.

91
00:05:00,269 --> 00:05:02,354
A bit like impersonating
an industry colleague

92
00:05:02,438 --> 00:05:03,981
to steal information.

93
00:05:04,857 --> 00:05:08,569
- You do love to act, don't you, Louis?
- [huffs]

94
00:05:08,652 --> 00:05:12,573
To think you went as far as to remove
your precious horns for the role.

95
00:05:12,656 --> 00:05:15,117
I expect no less from a true thespian.

96
00:05:16,410 --> 00:05:17,870
I know all about you.

97
00:05:17,953 --> 00:05:21,623
You're the first and only herbivore
to ever run the Shishi-Gumi

98
00:05:21,707 --> 00:05:23,834
after you killed their boss and took over.

99
00:05:23,917 --> 00:05:26,128
- You're wrong.
- Ah, forgive me.

100
00:05:26,670 --> 00:05:28,422
You're the ex-boss, aren't you?

101
00:05:28,505 --> 00:05:30,716
- [huffs]
- Relax.

102
00:05:31,216 --> 00:05:35,345
I have no intention of revealing
your sordid past to the world.

103
00:05:35,429 --> 00:05:36,263
Then...

104
00:05:36,346 --> 00:05:39,808
Their current boss is a character.

105
00:05:39,892 --> 00:05:41,894
- Do you know him?
- Of him.

106
00:05:41,977 --> 00:05:44,354
Do you know that Melon is a mix?

107
00:05:44,438 --> 00:05:45,272
Melon?

108
00:05:46,356 --> 00:05:49,276
- He's a gazelle and a carnivore?
- A leopard. Yes.

109
00:05:49,777 --> 00:05:52,112
[gasps] I thought as much.

110
00:05:52,196 --> 00:05:53,989
Incredible, right?

111
00:05:54,073 --> 00:05:55,616
Mixes are the one subject

112
00:05:55,699 --> 00:05:58,160
I'm most obsessed
with researching right now!

113
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,705
{\an8}Of course, it's natural
for one to take interest

114
00:06:01,789 --> 00:06:03,665
{\an8}in the beasts they come into contact with

115
00:06:03,749 --> 00:06:05,918
regardless of their sex or species.

116
00:06:06,001 --> 00:06:09,004
But for me, those differences
make them even more alluring.

117
00:06:09,588 --> 00:06:12,925
As a former Shishi-Gumi boss,
perhaps you can relate?

118
00:06:13,884 --> 00:06:16,553
Why are you so drawn to mixed beasts
in particular?

119
00:06:17,096 --> 00:06:21,558
Some mixes have extreme imbalances
in their senses or intuition or instincts.

120
00:06:22,101 --> 00:06:24,978
It's really quite extraordinary
to see that in action.

121
00:06:25,896 --> 00:06:28,398
- You're talking about super senses.
- Hmm.

122
00:06:29,191 --> 00:06:30,734
They can perceive sounds or light

123
00:06:30,818 --> 00:06:33,320
too faint to be measured
by scientific instruments,

124
00:06:33,403 --> 00:06:36,782
or they might completely lack
appetite or sexual desire.

125
00:06:36,865 --> 00:06:39,409
Do you think there's a connection
between senses and desires?

126
00:06:39,493 --> 00:06:42,162
Well, at the moment,
that's just a hypothesis.

127
00:06:42,746 --> 00:06:45,499
What I do know
is despite his slender build,

128
00:06:45,582 --> 00:06:48,752
Melon possesses a ferocity
that rivals even the lions'.

129
00:06:49,294 --> 00:06:52,005
Though I haven't collected any data
on his senses.

130
00:06:53,215 --> 00:06:55,092
Do you have any information?

131
00:06:55,717 --> 00:06:58,887
No, I've never had the pleasure
of meeting him.

132
00:06:58,971 --> 00:07:01,431
I see. That's unfortunate.

133
00:07:06,562 --> 00:07:07,729
[Louis] <i>He's not wrong.</i>

134
00:07:08,272 --> 00:07:11,692
<i>A lion should be able to overpower
that skinny creature easily.</i>

135
00:07:12,401 --> 00:07:14,653
<i>But he exudes an intense authority.</i>

136
00:07:14,736 --> 00:07:17,114
<i>Perhaps they were right
to be terrified of him.</i>

137
00:07:17,865 --> 00:07:20,659
<i>Something about him is unsettling.</i>

138
00:07:22,202 --> 00:07:24,204
[cell phone vibrating]

139
00:07:25,831 --> 00:07:28,625
CHLOE

140
00:07:29,334 --> 00:07:30,502
This is Louis.

141
00:07:30,586 --> 00:07:32,379
[Chloe] <i>Hey. How'd it go?</i>

142
00:07:33,046 --> 00:07:34,631
I found out the cause at least.

143
00:07:35,215 --> 00:07:39,303
Kines reacts with a substance that remains
in the body after meat consumption

144
00:07:39,386 --> 00:07:41,430
and stimulates the nervous system.

145
00:07:41,513 --> 00:07:43,098
<i>I was afraid of that.</i>

146
00:07:43,182 --> 00:07:44,933
<i>So, if someone has ever eaten meat,</i>

147
00:07:45,017 --> 00:07:47,811
<i>there's a possibility
they could become violent.</i>

148
00:07:47,895 --> 00:07:49,605
We need to deal with this at once.

149
00:07:49,688 --> 00:07:51,940
<i>Don't tell me
you want to confront the supplier.</i>

150
00:07:52,024 --> 00:07:53,859
<i>That's a tragedy waiting to happen.</i>

151
00:07:54,693 --> 00:07:56,111
No. Of course, you're right.

152
00:07:57,446 --> 00:07:59,448
[huffs] I have another idea.

153
00:08:04,077 --> 00:08:07,998
UDON BEBEBE

154
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:11,460
[Legoshi] I can't apologize enough.

155
00:08:13,253 --> 00:08:16,048
I mean that. I'm so sorry.

156
00:08:17,549 --> 00:08:18,550
Huh?

157
00:08:18,634 --> 00:08:19,801
[Sunaga] Leftovers.

158
00:08:19,885 --> 00:08:21,345
- Don't make me toss 'em.
- Huh?

159
00:08:22,095 --> 00:08:24,223
Well, okay.

160
00:08:25,224 --> 00:08:26,767
I appreciate it.

161
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:34,107
[Legoshi blowing, slurping]

162
00:08:34,858 --> 00:08:35,692
[sighs]

163
00:08:36,610 --> 00:08:39,154
Oh, that's good. I really needed this.

164
00:08:40,697 --> 00:08:42,533
Not that I want to lecture you,

165
00:08:43,075 --> 00:08:46,870
but in the future, I need you to call out
so I can make arrangements, okay?

166
00:08:46,954 --> 00:08:49,957
You can't just skip out work
without saying anything to your boss.

167
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,333
I'm sorry, sir.

168
00:08:51,416 --> 00:08:54,628
Now, what's all this about you
getting shot and killed by some big fruit?

169
00:08:54,711 --> 00:08:57,297
- Melon? That's his name.
- Never mind the name.

170
00:08:58,006 --> 00:09:00,217
You were shot and killed,
met up with your dead mother,

171
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,302
and then magically came back to life?

172
00:09:02,886 --> 00:09:04,304
Who's going to believe that?

173
00:09:04,388 --> 00:09:06,348
Everything I'm telling you is true.

174
00:09:07,349 --> 00:09:08,350
[Sunaga sighs]

175
00:09:09,476 --> 00:09:12,688
When you're finished, I need you to clean
the toilets and the exhaust vent.

176
00:09:13,564 --> 00:09:14,398
Got it.

177
00:09:16,984 --> 00:09:20,362
<i>So warm. Makes me glad to be alive.</i>

178
00:09:23,907 --> 00:09:27,327
[Yahya] Were you able to find
any of that Melda he was talking about?

179
00:09:27,411 --> 00:09:30,622
[Corne] Either it disappeared
or it <i>was</i> disappeared.

180
00:09:31,290 --> 00:09:34,001
And now this mask
is the only lead we have left.

181
00:09:34,793 --> 00:09:36,545
No attendee list to speak of,

182
00:09:37,212 --> 00:09:40,173
Legoshi is missing,
and Melon's in the wind.

183
00:09:40,257 --> 00:09:44,970
Well, have you considered the possibility
that the wolf may have tricked us?

184
00:09:45,053 --> 00:09:47,639
Mmm, you think he's an accomplice.

185
00:09:47,723 --> 00:09:49,433
He really was shot, you know.

186
00:09:49,516 --> 00:09:52,936
I know. But was the gun meant
for large beasts?

187
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,980
[gasps, sighs]

188
00:09:55,772 --> 00:09:57,774
- [elevator chimes]
- Hmm.

189
00:10:07,868 --> 00:10:09,953
Mr. Yahya, is there any news on Melon?

190
00:10:11,330 --> 00:10:14,291
To think my own wounds
have barely begun to heal,

191
00:10:14,374 --> 00:10:16,543
and you're all bright-eyed
and bush-tailed.

192
00:10:17,169 --> 00:10:19,671
- You really are something else, aren't ya?
- [chuckles]

193
00:10:19,755 --> 00:10:21,798
Well, I am Gosha's grandson.

194
00:10:21,882 --> 00:10:24,217
Oh! I'm so sorry. I'll come back.

195
00:10:24,301 --> 00:10:25,510
No, you can stay.

196
00:10:26,178 --> 00:10:29,556
Corne here has been my right hand
in the Melon investigation.

197
00:10:30,307 --> 00:10:33,518
Look at that. Not every day
I meet a fellow scarface.

198
00:10:33,602 --> 00:10:34,603
Good to meet you.

199
00:10:34,686 --> 00:10:37,189
Uh, right back at ya. My name's Legoshi.

200
00:10:38,315 --> 00:10:40,442
- [Yahya] Melon's gone, by the way.
- Hmm?

201
00:10:41,151 --> 00:10:44,529
I'm sorry. I even had him
right in front of me.

202
00:10:44,613 --> 00:10:45,572
It's fine.

203
00:10:46,448 --> 00:10:50,202
It's entirely my fault for involving
an amateur like you in the first place.

204
00:10:50,827 --> 00:10:54,164
I put you directly in harm's way.
Forgive me.

205
00:10:54,247 --> 00:10:57,209
Uh, no. I wouldn't have gone
if I didn't want to.

206
00:10:57,292 --> 00:10:58,627
That's not on you at all.

207
00:10:59,169 --> 00:11:01,421
Gosha was worried sick about you.

208
00:11:01,505 --> 00:11:03,340
Come on, you told my grandpa?

209
00:11:03,423 --> 00:11:06,760
Yeah. He really chewed me out
for this one.

210
00:11:08,095 --> 00:11:10,597
So you understand
why I can't involve you any further.

211
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:13,266
- But what if--
- This isn't up for discussion.

212
00:11:13,850 --> 00:11:16,937
We're not discussing.
I'm telling you I'm not done here.

213
00:11:17,521 --> 00:11:21,024
Listen, Melon can't get away.
I have to speak with him again.

214
00:11:21,691 --> 00:11:24,778
If you know where he is,
please just tell me.

215
00:11:24,861 --> 00:11:27,531
[inhales deeply] Hmm.

216
00:11:30,659 --> 00:11:32,744
We don't have any leads right now.

217
00:11:32,828 --> 00:11:33,995
Oh, I see.

218
00:11:34,079 --> 00:11:36,623
Besides, there's no talking
to a guy like that.

219
00:11:36,706 --> 00:11:38,583
Well, I can't know that unless I try.

220
00:11:39,209 --> 00:11:41,211
Right? I'll do it alone.

221
00:11:41,294 --> 00:11:42,546
[Legoshi grunts]

222
00:11:42,629 --> 00:11:43,630
Hey!

223
00:11:47,092 --> 00:11:48,343
[both] Hmm.

224
00:11:50,011 --> 00:11:51,430
[theater owner] Number ten...

225
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:55,559
Number 11, number 12.

226
00:11:56,935 --> 00:12:00,021
Good. Next is the cue light.

227
00:12:01,648 --> 00:12:02,899
[theater owner gasps]

228
00:12:02,983 --> 00:12:05,610
Hey! We're closed!
What are you doing in here?

229
00:12:06,194 --> 00:12:10,782
Pardon me. Is there any chance Miss Cosmo
or Miss Luna are here right now?

230
00:12:10,866 --> 00:12:11,950
[theater owner] What?

231
00:12:12,033 --> 00:12:15,579
Uh, if you have business with those girls,
you'd better give up.

232
00:12:15,662 --> 00:12:17,497
- They're not coming back.
- What?

233
00:12:17,581 --> 00:12:20,375
PERFORMANCE CANCELED

234
00:12:20,459 --> 00:12:25,213
So, um, regarding the person
who organized the party the other night--

235
00:12:25,297 --> 00:12:27,340
Let it go. Get lost already.

236
00:12:27,424 --> 00:12:30,218
I mean, any information would be helpful.

237
00:12:30,886 --> 00:12:33,180
- Oh. Your tail...
- [gasps]

238
00:12:33,263 --> 00:12:36,308
Mind your own business.
Quit bugging me, and get out of here!

239
00:12:36,391 --> 00:12:39,311
- I don't want to cause you any trouble.
- Get it through your thick skull!

240
00:12:39,394 --> 00:12:41,354
You're already causing me trouble,
you moron!

241
00:12:42,063 --> 00:12:45,484
{\an8}I lose my star performer,
my tail gets cut off...

242
00:12:45,567 --> 00:12:46,401
{\an8}[gasps]

243
00:12:47,319 --> 00:12:49,654
[Yahya] <i>And definitely don't mention
the investigation.</i>

244
00:12:49,738 --> 00:12:51,490
<i>You'll put the ladies in danger.</i>

245
00:12:53,575 --> 00:12:54,826
[Legoshi] <i>No.</i>

246
00:12:55,744 --> 00:12:59,873
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. I'll go now.

247
00:13:02,167 --> 00:13:05,212
- Uh, but one more thing before I do--
- Piss off already!

248
00:13:05,795 --> 00:13:07,881
The third light from the back,
it's burned out.

249
00:13:07,964 --> 00:13:08,798
Huh?

250
00:13:09,466 --> 00:13:11,051
[Legoshi] Sorry to have bothered you.

251
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,553
Oh, so it is.

252
00:13:16,097 --> 00:13:17,557
Hey, wolf boy.

253
00:13:18,350 --> 00:13:19,184
[Legoshi] Hmm?

254
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:23,146
Cosmo said she could see a strange pattern
through their shirt.

255
00:13:23,230 --> 00:13:24,231
The host, I mean.

256
00:13:26,024 --> 00:13:27,317
A strange pattern...

257
00:13:30,028 --> 00:13:31,363
[Legoshi groans]

258
00:13:34,491 --> 00:13:35,992
<i>A pattern, huh?</i>

259
00:13:37,244 --> 00:13:39,120
<i>I wonder... Hmm?</i>

260
00:13:40,914 --> 00:13:44,251
[snarls] What are you looking at?

261
00:13:44,334 --> 00:13:46,253
[gasps, hums]

262
00:13:47,963 --> 00:13:49,047
[exhales contentedly]

263
00:13:49,798 --> 00:13:53,718
Ocean creatures, they don't know
how lovely this feels.

264
00:13:53,802 --> 00:13:55,470
What a shame that is.

265
00:13:56,137 --> 00:13:58,098
So you've decided you like the bath?

266
00:13:58,181 --> 00:14:00,725
Yes, yes, I have at last.

267
00:14:00,809 --> 00:14:03,353
That's good.
You were a little scared at first.

268
00:14:03,436 --> 00:14:04,854
Indeed.

269
00:14:05,647 --> 00:14:08,525
But once you showed me,
I've grown to like them.

270
00:14:08,608 --> 00:14:10,735
Everyone is naked here.

271
00:14:10,819 --> 00:14:15,156
Even land animals who wear so much clothes
to protect themselves.

272
00:14:15,824 --> 00:14:18,493
In the bath, everyone is equal.

273
00:14:19,035 --> 00:14:21,913
We're all shedding
the constraints of society.

274
00:14:21,997 --> 00:14:23,039
Or something.

275
00:14:23,123 --> 00:14:24,791
Together, yes.

276
00:14:24,875 --> 00:14:27,168
And this way, we share our scars.

277
00:14:27,252 --> 00:14:28,712
- Many scars.
- [hesitates]

278
00:14:28,795 --> 00:14:29,963
Yeah, I...

279
00:14:30,046 --> 00:14:32,674
- [Legoshi] I've been through a lot.
- [Sagwan] That is life.

280
00:14:32,757 --> 00:14:33,717
Uh...

281
00:14:35,218 --> 00:14:38,388
But eating good food and taking a bath,

282
00:14:38,471 --> 00:14:41,641
you know, that's what makes me
feel like I'm living.

283
00:14:41,725 --> 00:14:42,767
[gasps, hesitates]

284
00:14:42,851 --> 00:14:45,979
Uh, please don't cry. Look, I'm all right.

285
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:49,649
These are not tears. It's bathwater.

286
00:14:49,733 --> 00:14:50,734
Oh, uh...

287
00:14:51,318 --> 00:14:54,279
In the sea, I've never cried before.

288
00:14:54,362 --> 00:14:57,407
Many fish die there, but it's no big deal.

289
00:14:58,074 --> 00:15:00,827
I don't cry, even when friends die.

290
00:15:01,661 --> 00:15:05,707
Although, my good friend Legoshi,

291
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:09,502
if you were to die,
I would surely cry on land.

292
00:15:09,586 --> 00:15:11,504
Oh, Mr. Sagwan...

293
00:15:12,589 --> 00:15:14,299
I will teach you.

294
00:15:14,382 --> 00:15:15,467
Listen.

295
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:19,054
If you are in trouble at sea,
just shout like this.

296
00:15:19,137 --> 00:15:20,096
[inhales deeply]

297
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,432
[blubbering]

298
00:15:22,515 --> 00:15:24,267
I, uh-- Wait a second. [inhales deeply]

299
00:15:24,351 --> 00:15:25,685
[blubbering]

300
00:15:26,269 --> 00:15:29,439
[speaking in ocean language]

301
00:15:29,522 --> 00:15:32,609
[speaking in ocean language]

302
00:15:33,985 --> 00:15:35,195
[gasps]

303
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,322
[in English] So, what does that mean?

304
00:15:37,405 --> 00:15:41,743
What it means is,
"I am Legoshi, the Great Gray Wolf."

305
00:15:41,826 --> 00:15:45,246
- Next, I'll teach you the magic words.
- [inhales deeply]

306
00:15:46,164 --> 00:15:50,210
[speaking in ocean language]

307
00:15:52,295 --> 00:15:53,630
[gasps]

308
00:15:54,631 --> 00:15:56,383
[in English] Okay, what does that mean?

309
00:15:56,466 --> 00:15:58,843
- That is secret.
- Uh, what?

310
00:15:58,927 --> 00:16:00,053
Please tell me.

311
00:16:00,845 --> 00:16:02,097
BATH HOUSE

312
00:16:02,597 --> 00:16:05,392
Mr. Sagwan. Come on, please?

313
00:16:08,228 --> 00:16:11,523
- What did you teach me how to say?
- Huh? [sniffs]

314
00:16:11,606 --> 00:16:13,191
That smells nice.

315
00:16:13,274 --> 00:16:16,194
[sniffs] Mmm, that does smell good.

316
00:16:16,277 --> 00:16:17,862
Hey, don't change the subject.

317
00:16:18,571 --> 00:16:19,447
[seller] Welcome.

318
00:16:20,156 --> 00:16:20,991
OCTOPUS

319
00:16:21,074 --> 00:16:22,158
Two orders, please.

320
00:16:22,242 --> 00:16:25,996
<i>- Capturing ocean creatures is a crime.</i>
- [seller] Two? That'll be 600.

321
00:16:26,079 --> 00:16:27,622
Mmm, I'll tell you what.

322
00:16:27,706 --> 00:16:28,957
Since you're an ocean creature,

323
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:32,419
why don't I cut you a special deal
and make it 650 even?

324
00:16:32,502 --> 00:16:34,004
That is very kind.

325
00:16:34,671 --> 00:16:37,674
Hey, Mr. Sagwan.
What are you doing? This is wrong.

326
00:16:37,757 --> 00:16:39,926
Oh, don't you worry. It's good.

327
00:16:40,010 --> 00:16:42,053
- [seller] Thanks for your patience.
- Uh...

328
00:16:42,804 --> 00:16:43,930
[Sagwan] Here is 600.

329
00:16:45,015 --> 00:16:47,726
Ooh! That looks tasty!

330
00:16:47,809 --> 00:16:49,894
- [sighs, gasps]
- [chomping]

331
00:16:49,978 --> 00:16:51,396
No, wait, you have to stop.

332
00:16:51,479 --> 00:16:54,357
You shouldn't be eating that.
It's a fellow sea creature, isn't it?

333
00:16:54,941 --> 00:16:56,151
[gulps, exhales]

334
00:16:56,234 --> 00:16:58,153
Legoshi, have you forgotten?

335
00:16:58,236 --> 00:17:02,365
In the sea,
everyone must eat and is eaten.

336
00:17:02,449 --> 00:17:04,534
It is just a fact of life.

337
00:17:04,617 --> 00:17:07,662
Uh, yeah. Maybe.

338
00:17:07,829 --> 00:17:10,290
- [hesitates] But don't you--
- [Sagwan] It is dead.

339
00:17:11,207 --> 00:17:14,085
That is all. It cannot come back.

340
00:17:15,795 --> 00:17:18,131
[chomping]

341
00:17:18,214 --> 00:17:19,966
Mmm. [chuckles]

342
00:17:20,050 --> 00:17:21,468
[Legoshi] <i>He's not wrong.</i>

343
00:17:22,677 --> 00:17:25,847
<i>It's just the food chain.
Logically, I get it.</i>

344
00:17:25,930 --> 00:17:28,975
<i>But when I see it right in front of me, I...</i>

345
00:17:29,059 --> 00:17:32,312
[Sagwan sighs] That is delicious!

346
00:17:32,395 --> 00:17:33,396
[Legoshi] <i>Hmm.</i>

347
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:37,776
Rather than an animal
who does not know the ways of the sea,

348
00:17:37,859 --> 00:17:39,736
I will eat this friend.

349
00:17:39,819 --> 00:17:42,489
That's better, right? What do you say?

350
00:17:42,572 --> 00:17:44,199
Mmm, I guess.

351
00:17:44,991 --> 00:17:48,828
Legoshi, you are kind. Very, very kind.

352
00:17:48,912 --> 00:17:50,080
[Legoshi] Hmm.

353
00:17:50,163 --> 00:17:52,290
But tasty things are tasty.

354
00:17:52,916 --> 00:17:54,459
Just like udon is.

355
00:17:54,542 --> 00:17:57,045
Well, udon isn't a living thing.

356
00:17:57,921 --> 00:17:59,923
Thank you for the meal, young man.

357
00:18:01,007 --> 00:18:03,093
Remember, poaching is illegal.

358
00:18:03,176 --> 00:18:04,886
[chuckles nervously]

359
00:18:04,969 --> 00:18:07,222
Mr. Sagwan, let's go. Come on.

360
00:18:07,305 --> 00:18:10,391
Well, you had no problem eating it,
you jackass! [huffs]

361
00:18:10,475 --> 00:18:12,977
[Melon] I think I'd like to give it a try,
if you don't mind?

362
00:18:13,853 --> 00:18:15,396
[gasps]

363
00:18:16,356 --> 00:18:19,150
- [Melon] I'll take one.
- [seller] Sure, that's 400.

364
00:18:25,198 --> 00:18:26,282
[chews] Hmm.

365
00:18:26,366 --> 00:18:31,079
[Melon] <i>I was robbed of the taste buds
of both herbivore and carnivore.</i>

366
00:18:32,288 --> 00:18:34,916
<i>No matter how much flavor I add,</i>

367
00:18:34,999 --> 00:18:37,752
<i>no matter when or what I eat,</i>

368
00:18:38,461 --> 00:18:41,506
<i>everything turns to ash in my mouth.</i>

369
00:18:42,757 --> 00:18:43,591
[spits]

370
00:18:47,804 --> 00:18:50,223
<i>I have no appetite, I have no libido,</i>

371
00:18:50,807 --> 00:18:54,686
<i>I can't expose my face or body to anyone
without terrifying them.</i>

372
00:18:55,979 --> 00:18:59,732
<i>There's only one place
I can truly reveal myself.</i>

373
00:18:59,816 --> 00:19:02,485
THE BLUE DRAGON

374
00:19:02,569 --> 00:19:04,571
[male staff] Oh, Mr. Melon!

375
00:19:04,654 --> 00:19:07,115
- Is that poky prick around?
- [laughs]

376
00:19:07,198 --> 00:19:10,076
Yeah, he sent another customer
to the hospital today.

377
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,119
[male staff laughs]

378
00:19:11,202 --> 00:19:13,997
I fired him,
but he'll be packing up for a while.

379
00:19:16,124 --> 00:19:17,458
[Melon] What's up, Holger?

380
00:19:19,544 --> 00:19:21,838
[slowly] Huh?

381
00:19:21,921 --> 00:19:25,091
You know, it's almost adorable
they're trying to label you of all beasts

382
00:19:25,175 --> 00:19:26,926
a psycho killer, isn't it?

383
00:19:27,010 --> 00:19:28,636
You're just too stinkin' slow and stupid

384
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:31,389
to realize when your clients
are bleeding to death.

385
00:19:31,931 --> 00:19:33,558
- [slowly] Huh.
- [gun cocks]

386
00:19:34,184 --> 00:19:37,228
Come on, pal, you have to be polite
like everyone else.

387
00:19:37,312 --> 00:19:39,689
- Put your heart in it.
- [slowly] Welcome in...

388
00:19:39,772 --> 00:19:40,899
[Melon] That's better.

389
00:19:40,982 --> 00:19:44,694
...my friend.

390
00:19:45,361 --> 00:19:48,281
[Melon sighs wearily]
Can you believe this shit?

391
00:19:49,032 --> 00:19:52,327
This leopard pattern
has finally spread down to my legs.

392
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:54,704
[sighs]

393
00:19:55,455 --> 00:19:56,623
The same as usual.

394
00:19:56,706 --> 00:20:01,044
Do your thing and fill in the foliage.
As many leaves as it takes to cover it.

395
00:20:01,794 --> 00:20:03,796
[whirring]

396
00:20:04,589 --> 00:20:07,342
NIMBLE

397
00:20:07,425 --> 00:20:10,261
[grunts, sighs heavily]

398
00:20:11,930 --> 00:20:13,765
[moaning]

399
00:20:18,269 --> 00:20:19,395
That hits the spot!

400
00:20:19,479 --> 00:20:20,563
[laughs]

401
00:20:20,647 --> 00:20:23,233
I'll never get tired of this feeling.

402
00:20:23,816 --> 00:20:26,736
[groaning] Right there!

403
00:20:26,819 --> 00:20:29,989
- [whirring]
- [Melon laughs maniacally]

404
00:20:30,073 --> 00:20:32,200
This pain is proof that I'm alive.

405
00:20:32,909 --> 00:20:34,118
Oh, yeah!

406
00:20:34,202 --> 00:20:37,497
The question is,
how long can I keep this up?

407
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:40,291
Or will I continue turning into a leopard?

408
00:20:40,375 --> 00:20:41,918
[groaning]

409
00:20:49,259 --> 00:20:51,469
[sniffs, sighs]

410
00:20:51,552 --> 00:20:53,554
[sniffing]

411
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,060
Huh? [sniffs]

412
00:21:00,770 --> 00:21:02,105
Excuse me.

413
00:21:02,730 --> 00:21:04,649
Hmm. [sniffs]

414
00:21:06,025 --> 00:21:07,986
[sniffing]

415
00:21:11,030 --> 00:21:12,115
Hmm.

416
00:21:13,783 --> 00:21:14,617
[sniffs]

417
00:21:20,039 --> 00:21:21,374
<i>Was I too late?</i>

418
00:21:22,917 --> 00:21:23,876
[gasps]

419
00:21:24,711 --> 00:21:26,004
- [gasps]
- [laughs]

420
00:21:26,087 --> 00:21:28,881
Sorry about that, buddy.
I didn't see you come in.

421
00:21:28,965 --> 00:21:31,301
Oh, shit, don't worry,
nobody died in here.

422
00:21:31,926 --> 00:21:34,387
The previous client
just bled a lot is all.

423
00:21:34,887 --> 00:21:39,100
[Holger speaking slowly]
Be careful with that gun.

424
00:21:39,684 --> 00:21:42,020
- Uh, gun?
- [laughs] Not you.

425
00:21:42,103 --> 00:21:45,315
His slow ass is still
working on responding to the last guy.

426
00:21:45,398 --> 00:21:49,027
Put it away,

427
00:21:49,569 --> 00:21:52,905
Mr. Melon.

428
00:21:53,489 --> 00:21:55,825
[Legoshi] <i>He's talking to Melon.</i>

429
00:21:55,908 --> 00:21:58,036
[mysterious piano music playing]

430
00:21:58,119 --> 00:21:59,746
<i>Guess I should let him finish.</i>

431
00:21:59,829 --> 00:22:00,913
[music fades]

432
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

433
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

434
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,296
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

435
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,467
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

436
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,803
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

437
00:22:17,805 --> 00:22:20,558
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

438
00:22:21,142 --> 00:22:23,603
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

439
00:22:23,686 --> 00:22:26,230
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

440
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,527
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

441
00:22:32,612 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

442
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

443
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,791
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

444
00:22:44,874 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

445
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,044
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

446
00:22:48,127 --> 00:22:52,590
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

447
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,552
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

448
00:22:56,636 --> 00:23:00,765
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

449
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,767
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

450
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,227
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

451
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

452
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

453
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,693
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

454
00:23:13,402 --> 00:23:16,322
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

455
00:23:17,365 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

456
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,372
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

457
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:28,918
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
